;;; A bare `_` inside a nested fact is dropped at load, in silence — M1f
;;; **W29**, register row `W29/nested-fact-arg` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; banked by S1f.5.0 (2026-11-08) from S1f.5.1's case (the inventory of
;;; 2026-11-06's W-22), filed `open` and owned by S1f.5.1, on the user's
;;; ruling of 2026-11-06 (Q-M1e2.22).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One fact whose first argument is the nested fact `(f _ a)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A bare `_` is reserved and names nothing, at any depth (Q-M1e2.22), so the
;;; program is refused at load, with a line naming the place: every command
;;; that reads it exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The loader drops the `_` and stores `(r (f a) c)`, with no line (`ein
;;; saturate FILE --dump`). Root's state is `(model (r (f a) c))` and R is four
;;; states, over the candidates `(r a c)` and `(r c a)`, exit 0 (`ein solve
;;; FILE` and `ein oracle FILE` at `ec004a48`, the engine `916d97ac`'s, release
;;; and debug alike).

(relation r T T)
(r (f _ a) c)
